{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-v995-44v6-5fqm","published":"2026-11-10T20:52:38Z","modified":"2026-11-10T21:00:04.025096383Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-126062"],"summary":"JRuby: NONET is bypassed for external DTDs and entities when the systemId uses a short-form IPv4 host","details":"### Summary\n\nOn JRuby, the `NONET` parse option did not block an external DTD or entity whose system identifier used a short-form IPv4 host, such as `http://127.1/` or `http://169.254.43518/`, or was an absolute path such as `/x.dtd` in a document parsed from a network URL. An application that parses untrusted XML with `DTDLOAD`, `DTDVALID` or `NOENT` could be made to send network requests, potentially enabling SSRF.\n\nNokogiri 1.19.5 applies the `XML::Schema` check from [GHSA-8678-w3jw-xfc2](https://github.com/sparklemotion/nokogiri/security/advisories/GHSA-8678-w3jw-xfc2): with `NONET` set, only local resources are loaded.\n\nOnly JRuby is affected. Default parse options are not affected.\n\n### Severity\n\nThe Nokogiri maintainers have evaluated this as low severity.\n\n### Mitigation\n\nUpgrade to Nokogiri 1.19.5 or later, or do not enable `DTDLOAD`, `DTDVALID` or `NOENT` for untrusted input.\n\n### Credit\n\nThis issue was responsibly reported by @arpitjain099.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nokogiri","ecosystem":"RubyGems","purl":"pkg:gem/nokogiri"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.19.5"}]}],"versions":["1.0.0","1.0.1","1.0.2","1.0.3","1.0.4","1.0.5","1.0.6","1.0.7","1.1.0","1.1.1","1.10.0","1.10.0.rc1","1.10.1","1.10.10","1.10.2","1.10.3","1.10.4","1.10.5","1.10.6","1.10.7","1.10.8","1.10.9","1.11.0","1.11.0.rc1","1.11.0.rc2","1.11.0.rc3","1.11.0.rc4","1.11.1","1.11.2","1.11.3","1.11.4","1.11.5","1.11.6","1.11.7","1.12.0","1.12.0.rc1","1.12.1","1.12.2","1.12.3","1.12.4","1.12.5","1.13.0","1.13.1","1.13.10","1.13.2","1.13.3","1.13.4","1.13.5","1.13.6","1.13.7","1.13.8","1.13.9","1.14.0","1.14.0.rc1","1.14.1","1.14.2","1.14.3","1.14.4","